d a pretty  typical post for him he said thank you  disney plus for adding brothers in arms  deadpool movie and logan as the first  rated r movies on the platform while  your choice is questionable we'll take  it and of course he shared a picture of  him hugging ryan reynolds in the  deadpool suit a very nice post a very  warm post a thankful post and then  there's ryan reynolds who is just the  best and of course in his true sarcastic  way he says we're supposed to announce  logan and deadpool will soon be the  first r-rated movies on disney plus but  we all know some disney movies should  already be rated r for irreversible  trauma then he shows and of course these  are made by him they're not real but he  shows some r ratings for some old disney  movies including old yeller and bambi  one says cold-blooded killing of an  innocent deer mom that will cause  lifelong trauma the other one says rated  r for totally ugly cry inducing straight  up murder of old yeller also bear abuse  so in true ryan reynolds fashion he  announced that logan and the deadpool  films will be on disney plus and will be  their first rated r properties and what  i find very interesting about this is  that they are releasing these on disney  plus the day before the marvel studios  hall h panel at san diego comic con  where we are expecting a lot maybe we  shouldn't be expecting a lot but this is  very coincidental now we've talked about  comic con a lot and what to expect so i  won't dive too much into that but keep  in mind that d23 is also only a couple  of months away and based off of the  reports that we've been hearing marvel  studios is actually saving quite a bit  for d23 however this doesn't mean that  there aren't going to be any  announcements made at sdcc because keep  in mind hall age is typically where all  of the big stuff from marvel studios is  revealed is announced and if they don't  announce anything or give us any type of  reveal at all a lot of people are going  to be pretty disappointed now keep your  expectations in check i would not expect  everything to be revealed and i want to  expect super huge things like x-men and  the fantastic four and blade and all of  this other stuff but expect some i would  expect a couple of big reveals and some  release dates and maybe some projects  that haven't been announced yet as well  but just keep in mind that disney's d23  is coming up in a couple of months and  they do have to save some big  announcements for that as well so both  events should be very very exciting and  again it's pretty coincidental that  they're releasing deadpool deadpool 2  and logan on disney plus the day before  the hall h marvel studios panel at comic  con so we'll wait and see what happens  and if you want to stay up to date with  sdcc be sure to subscribe so you don't  miss out on any of the latest news for  live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof  you

